# ---- a remote docker host for the test runner (optional) --------------------
# bin/run-tests-in-docker.sh builds one image and runs the suite in containers.
# Ten of those at once on a Mac take the load past 120 and the kernel starts
# SIGKILLing them, which is why the local drain's agent limiter sits at 5 agents
# and 3 builds. DOCKER_HOST points the runner at a machine with spare RAM — a
# Fly machine, or any box with docker and ssh — so the Mac orchestrates and runs
# no container of its own.
#
# Set it here and every suite run on this box uses that daemon; a value already
# in the environment (`DOCKER_HOST=… bin/run-tests-in-docker.sh`) wins over this
# file, the way every other docker tool behaves. bin/lib/docker-host.sh is the
# one place either is read.
#
# A remote endpoint changes how the tree gets there: a bind mount resolves on
# the DAEMON's host, so the runner stages the checkout with rsync and copies it
# into the container instead. rsync has to be on PATH. The image is built on the
# remote host on the first run and kept there.
#
# AN ENDPOINT THAT DOES NOT ANSWER IS EXIT 2, not a quiet local run: falling
# back would put the containers straight back on the machine this knob exists to
# take them off, and nobody reads a warning. Unset it to go back to local.
#
# The operator steps to stand a host up, and what this costs, are in
# docs/notes/2026-09-22-BH-1193-remote-docker-host.md. bin/remote-gate.sh is the
# other way to the same relief (ssh + rsync to the shared Fly test host, no
# docker on either end) — see docs/REMOTE-GATE.md.
#DOCKER_HOST=ssh://root@<host>
#DOCKER_HOST=tcp://<host>:2375
